# fixedbugs, defect 2320, 2026-11-08: a group record of fixed-array fields,
# built once by a construction naming each, cost `heroes build` near the
# square of its fields. A fixed array has no storage in C and is rendered
# where it is used from the instruction that made it, and
# `emit/storageless.hero`'s `fixed_text` and `emit/gate.hero`'s
# `is_a_written_literal` each found that instruction by walking the whole
# function, for each argument of the construction. Each value's first
# writer is now found once per function (`emit/defined.hero`). The
# compiler's own instructions building N `u8[2]` fields at 2,048, 4,096 and
# 8,192: 21.62, 61.39 and 198.35 billion on the trunk's compiler, 11.98,
# 22.92 and 44.74 after. This program, 2,048 fields, an odd one holding
# `n + 1` where an even one holds `n`: 26.05 billion before, 13.22 after.
extern "fixedbugs-2320-a-group-record-of-two-thousand-fixed-array-fields-builds-in-linear-work.h"
